**Primary reviewer: Troy Goode.** They hold 144 of the 214 non-blank lines in `lib/index.js` (67.3%), or 159 of 238 counting blank lines (66.8%). They are the only active owner, with a last commit on 2026-04-10.

That figure counts two addresses as one person: `<email redacted>` (132 lines) and `troy@laptop.example` (12 lines). The merge is a guess from names and addresses, and nothing was written to `.mailmap`. Unmerged, the Gmail address alone holds 132 lines.

**Second reviewers.** None of the other owners has committed in the year before 2026-04-12, so none is active:
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson:** 20 lines (9.3%), or 22 counting blank lines (9.2%). Last commit to the file was 2017-10-04, though they committed elsewhere in the repo as late as 2021-09-07.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades:** 14 lines (6.5%), or 16 counting blank lines (6.7%). Last commit was 2015-05-28, and the tool counts their `alex94puchades` name as the same person. It credits them with 11 lines of e64e854, which Troy Goode committed.

Neither holds half of any file. 19 more authors hold the remaining lines.

**Risk.** The bus factor for this file is 1 on both bases: Troy alone passes 50% of the lines. It takes 3 authors to reach 80%. Active people hold 67.3% of the lines, so 32.7% belong to people with no recent commit. This counts surviving lines, not who understands the code. The tool found no orphaned files here.

**Left out.** Merge commits are credited to the authors on the merged branches. The history starts with an import on 2013-01-30, so older lines go to whoever imported them. The tool examined 34 commits and set aside none. It flagged one commit as possibly mechanical but did not exclude it: fcd2b56 "issue #42: (WIP) switch to ESLint; clean up" by Troy Goode, with 6 surviving lines. That is too small to change the ranking. The earlier 4-space/double-quote reformat commit 62628c0 was already ignored through `.git-blame-ignore-revs`.

